<p>Brazil has revoked the visa of Darren Beattie, a U.S. State Department adviser on Brazil policy, after he sought to travel there to meet former President Jair Bolsonaro, according to reports published on March 13 and 14. President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva said Brazil barred Beattie from entering the country. The dispute has added to already strained relations between Brasilia and Washington.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/85ZhQqDCRCDICDiN9EsmCZwCPtgOgdSryMD9P0_Ux7ze5r219ghFGompjj1bdktPeqxRN46u9FYnicSg2S5srFPSinFngUISvJHDOJ2jG0qX1Khy0NJ6R6W922k6zXcClGBjBu9NoDmKQ6nUrekeQ8wAP2KxKjn9gQTvDqu7snf29ghJFinRIshSeMNoRuiPDo9AoDw' alt='Darren Beattie, the State Department adviser on Brazil policy whose planned trip became the center of the visa dispute.' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Brazilian government: Officials tied the visa cancellation to U.S. visa penalties imposed on some Brazilian officials in August, presenting Brazil&#x27;s move as a reciprocal response. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/brazil-revokes-us-official-darren-beatties-visa-in-reciprocal-measure/article70742382.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva: Lula said Beattie could not visit Bolsonaro in prison, making that planned stop the center of the dispute. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/13/brazil-pulls-visa-of-trump-adviser-who-asked-to-visit-bolsonaro-in-prison'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Brazilian critics of U.S. involvement: People cited by The New York Times said Beattie&#x27;s planned meetings with Bolsonaro allies fueled fears that Washington could meddle in Brazil&#x27;s next election. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/13/world/middleeast/brazil-election-darren-beattie-trump.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/brazil-revokes-us-official-darren-beatties-visa-in-reciprocal-measure/article70742382.ece'>Brazil revokes U.S. official Darren 